WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
In 1933, unemployment in the United
States reached about 25 per cent.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.360
After the war, governments
learned to keep jobs plentiful

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.210
by managing total spending in the economy.

4
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.170
Then, in 1973, oil prices
roughly quadrupled.

5
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:22.140
By 1975, UK inflation
was about 27 per cent.

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.660
The old cure had stopped working.

7
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.940
So why can the right cure for one slump

8
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.270
be the wrong cure for the next?

9
00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.500
In this mission, you'll
follow a century of crises,

10
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.900
from the 1930s to the crash of 2008.

11
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.200
Then you'll use a graph lab
to mix spending and money,

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.440
and watch output, prices
and interest rates.

13
00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.680
Your mission: find out why each
crisis needed its own cure.
